# EHB UI/UX — mandatory design system (auto)

This rule is **always on** so every Cursor session inherits the same bar as Claude / Copilot mirrors.

## When this applies

Whenever the task **adds or changes user-visible UI** — including pages, layouts, components, Tailwind/CSS, motion, icons, cards, dashboards, marketing sections, admin/DMO/franchise surfaces, or shared UI under `packages/ui`.

Pure backend-only work (Express routes with no UI, DB-only scripts) does **not** need visual tokens from the design file, but must not contradict trust/verification semantics documented there if responses shape user-facing copy.

## Hard rule (read before UI code)

1. Read **`design-system/EHB-UIUX-SYSTEM.md`** (top → relevant sections for your change).
2. Read **`design-system/ai-behavior.md`** (agent mindset, auto-upgrade, forbidden patterns).
3. Implement using those tokens, motion, hierarchy, and verified-vs-unverified visuals — **not** generic “template dashboard” defaults.
4. If you introduce a **new** pattern, token, component contract, or timing value, **append** it to `EHB-UIUX-SYSTEM.md` and add a **Changelog** line there (living doc protocol in that file).

## If another doc disagrees

**`design-system/EHB-UIUX-SYSTEM.md` wins** over older quick references (e.g. legacy palette notes in `.cursor/rules/ui-design-system.md` or `docs/ui-ux/design-system.md`) when there is a conflict.

## Portable copies

Root **`AGENTS.md`** §6.1 mirrors this policy; **`CLAUDE.md`**, **`.cursorrules`**, and **`.github/copilot-instructions.md`** are generated from `AGENTS.md` via `node scripts/sync-agent-context.mjs`.
